WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.189 --> 00:00:02.856
(playful music)

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:23.871
- Maybe you want to open
the conversation with

00:00:23.871 --> 00:00:25.270
inquiring about pronouns.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.101
- With kindness and love.

00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:29.032
- I think there's nothing
more frustrating than

00:00:29.032 --> 00:00:31.215
someone just seeing you
as the sum of your gender.

00:00:31.215 --> 00:00:32.918
- You would address a trans person

00:00:32.918 --> 00:00:34.491
like you would address any other person,

00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:35.900
you would treat them as a person.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.778
- You just say "hi."

00:00:37.778 --> 00:00:39.068
Start with that.

00:00:39.068 --> 00:00:41.735
(upbeat music)

00:00:44.072 --> 00:00:46.826
- Everybody has their
own nuanced definition

00:00:46.826 --> 00:00:48.792
of what transness means to them.

00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:51.175
- It's basically identifying as

00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:53.678
a gender that you were
not assigned at birth.

00:00:53.678 --> 00:00:56.196
- Being born in the gender that I

00:00:56.196 --> 00:00:58.090
really just don't fell comfortable in.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.562
- If you're gonna give
it a name, strength.

00:00:59.562 --> 00:01:01.126
I believe that us transgendered women,

00:01:01.126 --> 00:01:03.735
we have a strength unlike any other.

00:01:03.735 --> 00:01:06.318
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.028 --> 00:01:10.562
- A trans person looks like
any other type of person.

00:01:10.562 --> 00:01:12.225
That's like asking what
does a man look like?

00:01:12.225 --> 00:01:13.369
Or what does a woman look like,

00:01:13.369 --> 00:01:14.698
or what does a child look like?

00:01:14.698 --> 00:01:16.249
There are so many variables.

00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:19.666
- Trans people come in all genders, all--

00:01:20.882 --> 00:01:22.213
- [Both] Shapes and sizes.

00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:24.237
- All colors, and also, you know,

00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:27.250
you don't need to have
transitioned to be transgender.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.034
Trans people aren't
necessarily always visible.

00:01:30.034 --> 00:01:31.496
- Everybody's got a certain look.

00:01:31.496 --> 00:01:33.025
There's no particular uniform.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.917
- Just like all cis
women don't look alike,

00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.666
all trans women don't look alike.

00:01:36.666 --> 00:01:37.816
- I mean, look at you and I, honey.

00:01:37.816 --> 00:01:40.983
Only thing we share is a little mocha.

00:01:42.286 --> 00:01:44.438
- My transition was an evolution.

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:47.244
I knew from an early age
that I felt something.

00:01:47.244 --> 00:01:49.116
I didn't have the
language to articulate it.

00:01:49.116 --> 00:01:51.899
- I think there's always
been an element of me

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:53.069
that always knew.

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:57.491
- I knew at 19 that it was
possible to transition,

00:01:57.491 --> 00:01:59.887
and I didn't transition until 35.

00:01:59.887 --> 00:02:01.988
- Like you said, everyone's
journey is completely different.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.264
I mean, I always knew.

00:02:03.264 --> 00:02:05.332
- I was attracted to feminine things

00:02:05.332 --> 00:02:07.831
when I was around five,
but my parents didn't know,

00:02:07.831 --> 00:02:11.272
I didn't even know the
term trans or transgender.

00:02:11.272 --> 00:02:15.120
I was just told, "no, you
shouldn't be into Barbies,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.124
"you should be into GI Joe."

00:02:17.124 --> 00:02:19.319
- I was into My Little Pony.

00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:21.902
(upbeat music)

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.177
- Not all transgender
people are heterosexual

00:02:28.177 --> 00:02:30.368
and neither are they all gay.

00:02:30.368 --> 00:02:32.357
- Gender and sexuality
are not the same thing.

00:02:32.357 --> 00:02:35.076
- I've always been about beauty
doesn't have a sex for me,

00:02:35.076 --> 00:02:37.023
so at the end of the day, it's
like what I'm gonna remember

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.356
is whether or not you are a nice person.

00:02:43.325 --> 00:02:45.559
- Not all trans people take hormones

00:02:45.559 --> 00:02:47.196
or decide to take hormones.

00:02:47.196 --> 00:02:48.540
- I'm like "give it to me, baby."

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.575
- I love my 'mones.

00:02:49.575 --> 00:02:52.039
- A year into my recognition to myself,

00:02:52.039 --> 00:02:54.415
I was just like, this is
everything that I've always known,

00:02:54.415 --> 00:02:56.143
but brought it together,
like it brought my levels

00:02:56.143 --> 00:02:57.472
and everything together, so in a sense,

00:02:57.472 --> 00:02:58.783
it brought me right for my blood type.

00:02:58.783 --> 00:03:00.464
- Some trans people choose to use hormones

00:03:00.464 --> 00:03:04.072
because they want to have
masculinizing characteristics

00:03:04.072 --> 00:03:06.723
added to their body, or they want to have

00:03:06.723 --> 00:03:09.375
feminizing characteristics in their body

00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:12.625
and they don't naturally produce those.

00:03:14.806 --> 00:03:17.571
- Being trans does not
require having surgery.

00:03:17.571 --> 00:03:18.935
- So you kind are like forced,

00:03:18.935 --> 00:03:20.419
like okay, I need to
have all these surgeries

00:03:20.419 --> 00:03:22.781
so I can blend in and
people can accept me,

00:03:22.781 --> 00:03:24.743
but really, I didn't have to
have any of the surgeries,

00:03:24.743 --> 00:03:26.491
I just needed to love
myself and be accepted.

00:03:26.491 --> 00:03:28.052
- Everyone's journey
is completely different

00:03:28.052 --> 00:03:31.810
and I think that how you
feel inside is exactly that,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.948
and if you feel like
you've got to do something

00:03:33.948 --> 00:03:37.005
to make that inside
feel right, then you do.

00:03:37.005 --> 00:03:39.360
- It's all about the process of

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.923
changing your body if you
want to to make yourself

00:03:41.923 --> 00:03:44.883
feel more comfortable and
peaceful within your own mind.

00:03:44.883 --> 00:03:47.169
- You can be trans and never
have any type of surgery,

00:03:47.169 --> 00:03:48.350
never do anything at all,

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.987
maybe just change your
name, change your pronouns.

00:03:50.987 --> 00:03:53.787
You can do whatever, you can self-define.

00:03:53.787 --> 00:03:56.204
(calm music)

00:03:57.231 --> 00:03:59.885
- Dating while trans is a nightmare.

00:03:59.885 --> 00:04:01.756
It is so annoying.

00:04:01.756 --> 00:04:05.188
I mean, it's not like
there's not people out there,

00:04:05.188 --> 00:04:07.643
it's just a mine field.

00:04:07.643 --> 00:04:12.008
- Either extreme fetishism
or extreme rejection,

00:04:12.008 --> 00:04:13.615
there's really no middle ground for me.

00:04:13.615 --> 00:04:15.979
- Assertive woman is very different

00:04:15.979 --> 00:04:18.626
than being a touchy-feely guy.

00:04:18.626 --> 00:04:21.303
Now I'm a creep, so I had
to like learn all of those

00:04:21.303 --> 00:04:23.380
kind of nuanced behavior patterns.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.507
- A lot of guys that approach
me assume that I am cis,

00:04:26.507 --> 00:04:28.223
so do I tell him immediately?

00:04:28.223 --> 00:04:30.335
Do I tell him via text, do I call him?

00:04:30.335 --> 00:04:31.907
Do we meet up at Starbucks?

00:04:31.907 --> 00:04:33.839
It's so much that runs through my mind

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:36.507
as far as, okay, this man is feeling me,

00:04:36.507 --> 00:04:40.652
how am I going to
deliver this news to him?

00:04:40.652 --> 00:04:43.699
- It's scary because
you're going to a situation

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:46.833
where someone doesn't
necessarily know your background,

00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:49.906
and I don't fear for myself necessarily,

00:04:49.906 --> 00:04:52.048
but for trans women,

00:04:52.048 --> 00:04:54.704
that's a very dangerous
situation to be in.

00:04:54.704 --> 00:04:57.204
You know, women do get killed.

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.400
- My first thought is we're
not accepted by society.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.687
- That is a very good question.

00:05:04.687 --> 00:05:06.107
Why do black people get murdered?

00:05:06.107 --> 00:05:08.099
Why is anyone out there coming outside

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:10.449
with their face crooked,
taking someone else's life

00:05:10.449 --> 00:05:12.528
because of whatever it is
that they're going through?

00:05:12.528 --> 00:05:15.687
- Trans women of color are
being murdered left and right

00:05:15.687 --> 00:05:18.659
and they're not getting
the same opportunity as

00:05:18.659 --> 00:05:21.278
a cis person or a cis white person.

00:05:21.278 --> 00:05:23.531
- The reality of the matter is

00:05:23.531 --> 00:05:27.635
a lot of the murders are
based in stigma and shame.

00:05:27.635 --> 00:05:29.219
- There's a lot of fear in

00:05:29.219 --> 00:05:30.735
who does this person make me,

00:05:30.735 --> 00:05:32.880
and what does it say about my masculinity

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.964
and who I am in front of everybody else.

00:05:35.964 --> 00:05:38.873
- There's so many reasons
why trans women are murdered,

00:05:38.873 --> 00:05:41.759
but ultimately it comes down to prejudice.

00:05:41.759 --> 00:05:43.741
It comes to inequality,

00:05:43.741 --> 00:05:46.455
and it comes to lack of understanding

00:05:46.455 --> 00:05:50.471
about trans people and the
men that find us attractive.

00:05:50.471 --> 00:05:53.054
(upbeat music)

00:05:53.974 --> 00:05:55.690
- Of course you can be religious.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.532
I identify and believe in Buddhism

00:05:58.532 --> 00:06:01.436
and I've practiced that
since I was a child.

00:06:01.436 --> 00:06:03.935
- Religion's meant to be for everybody.

00:06:03.935 --> 00:06:05.366
- Anybody can be religious.

00:06:05.366 --> 00:06:06.991
- Anybody can be religious.
(laughs)

00:06:06.991 --> 00:06:09.532
- Transitioning was like a
spiritual experience for me.

00:06:09.532 --> 00:06:12.104
I finally felt like I was my whole self,

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.372
and as a result, I found
a relationship with

00:06:14.372 --> 00:06:17.121
a higher power of my understanding.

00:06:17.121 --> 00:06:19.538
(calm music)

00:06:20.826 --> 00:06:22.523
- The way that my mind is formed

00:06:22.523 --> 00:06:24.844
has been a blessing and that's, um,

00:06:24.844 --> 00:06:26.701
a lot of that is down to being trans

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:29.399
and empathizing, and coming into contact

00:06:29.399 --> 00:06:31.347
with so many amazing
people that I don't know

00:06:31.347 --> 00:06:32.861
if I would have met if I was cis.

00:06:32.861 --> 00:06:34.271
- Being able to look at yourself

00:06:34.271 --> 00:06:36.627
and, because you have to, a lot of times,

00:06:36.627 --> 00:06:38.979
you're like, why am I different?

00:06:38.979 --> 00:06:40.587
What is wrong with me?

00:06:40.587 --> 00:06:43.643
And so you spend a lot
of time thinking about

00:06:43.643 --> 00:06:44.476
who you are.

00:06:44.476 --> 00:06:45.720
- I love being trans.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:49.185
Having a human experience,
and I got to be both sexes.

00:06:49.185 --> 00:06:51.651
- At the end of the day,
none of us are worth anything

00:06:51.651 --> 00:06:52.828
if we don't love ourself.

00:06:52.828 --> 00:06:54.586
That has everything
with how it is that you

00:06:54.586 --> 00:06:56.774
hold your head up and how proud you are.

00:06:56.774 --> 00:06:58.636
- The thing I love most about being trans

00:06:58.636 --> 00:07:01.593
is getting this complete 360-degree view

00:07:01.593 --> 00:07:03.895
of what it means to be a human being.

00:07:03.895 --> 00:07:06.400
- But what I love most
about being trans for myself

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.319
has just been my journey
throughout womanhood

00:07:09.319 --> 00:07:11.803
and sharing stories
with fellow trans women

00:07:11.803 --> 00:07:15.335
and even cis women and seeing
differences and similarities.

00:07:15.335 --> 00:07:17.864
- I love that people are
googling these questions,

00:07:17.864 --> 00:07:20.812
because that means you're
curious and you want to learn

00:07:20.812 --> 00:07:22.375
something about the trans community.

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:25.355
- You can find out more that
you ever will on google,

00:07:25.355 --> 00:07:27.919
I swear, by actually speaking to people.

00:07:27.919 --> 00:07:30.336
(calm music)

